#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:5600 
msgid ""
"Performs a federated search on one or more valid federated providers that"
" is scoped to the \\\n"
"federated search string. A federated provider is valid when it represents"
" a remote Splunk \\\n"
"platform deployment, has an active configuration in federated.conf, and "
"the user who runs or \\\n"
"owns the search has valid role-based access permissions for the provider "
"as defined in authorize.conf. \\p\\\\\n"
"Use square brackets to specify the federated search string. The "
"'federate' command runs the entire \\\n"
"scoped federated search on each valid provider and collates the results. "
"When 'federate' \\\n"
"runs the scoped federated search on a transparent mode provider, it uses "
"knowledge objects \\\n"
"from the federated search head for the search. When 'federate' runs the "
"scoped federated \\\n"
"search on a standard mode provider or local provider, it uses knowledge "
"objects from the \\\n"
"remote search head for the search. The \"local\" provider is a special "
"provider that represents \\\n"
"the Splunk deployment from which the federated search is run.\\p\\\\\n"
"The optional 'use_fsh_ko' argument overrides knowledge object targeting "
"for all providers \\\n"
"in the command. When 'use_fsh_ko=true', the search uses knowledge objects"
" on the federated \\\n"
"search head. The provider must have 'useFSHKnowledgeObjects=true' "
"configured in federated.conf, \\\n"
"and bundle replication must already be turned on. \\p\\\\\n"
"When 'use_fsh_ko=false', the search uses knowledge objects on the remote "
"search head regardless \\\n"
"of the provider configuration. \\p\\\\\n"
"When 'use_fsh_ko' is not specified, the search uses the "
"'useFSHKnowledgeObjects' setting in \\\n"
"federated.conf for each provider by default. \\p\\\\\n"
"The 'local search string' in the search can be any commands that are run "
"locally on the federated \\\n"
"search head that receive the results from the federate command as input."
msgstr ""
"对一个或多个有效的联合提供程序执行联合搜索，该搜索的范围限定为 \\\n"
"联合搜索字符串。当联合提供程序代表远程 Splunk \\\n"
"platform 部署、在 federated.conf 中具有有效的活动配置，并且运行或 \\\n"
"拥有该搜索的用户按 authorize.conf 中的定义对该提供程序具有有效的基于角色的访问权限时，该联合提供程序即为有效。\\p\\\\\n"
"使用方括号指定联合搜索字符串。'federate' 命令会在每个有效提供程序上运行整个 \\\n"
"范围限定的联合搜索，并汇总结果。当 'federate' \\\n"
"在透明模式提供程序上运行范围限定的联合搜索时，它会使用来自联合 \\\n"
"搜索头的知识对象进行搜索。当 'federate' \\\n"
"在标准模式提供程序或本地提供程序上运行范围限定的联合 \\\n"
"搜索时，它会使用来自远程 \\\n"
"搜索头的知识对象进行搜索。“local” 提供程序是一种特殊 \\\n"
"提供程序，表示运行联合搜索的 Splunk 部署。\\p\\\\\n"
"可选的 'use_fsh_ko' 参数会覆盖该命令中所有提供程序的 \\\n"
"知识对象定位。当 'use_fsh_ko=true' 时，搜索会使用位于联合 \\\n"
"搜索头上的知识对象。提供程序必须在 federated.conf 中配置 'useFSHKnowledgeObjects=true'，\\\n"
"并且必须已启用 bundle replication。\\p\\\\\n"
"当 'use_fsh_ko=false' 时，无论提供程序配置如何，搜索都会使用远程 \\\n"
"搜索头上的知识对象。\\p\\\\\n"
"当未指定 'use_fsh_ko' 时，默认情况下，搜索会对每个提供程序使用 \\\n"
"federated.conf 中的 'useFSHKnowledgeObjects' 设置。\\p\\\\\n"
"搜索中的“本地搜索字符串”可以是任何在联合 \\\n"
"搜索头上本地运行并将 federate 命令的结果作为输入接收的命令。"

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:1314 
msgid ""
"Performs an arbitrary expression evaluation, providing mathematical, "
"string, and boolean operations. The results of eval are written to a "
"specified destination field, which can be a new or existing field. If the"
" destination field exists, the values of the field are replaced by the "
"results of eval. The syntax of the expression is checked before running "
"the search, and an exception will be thrown for an invalid expression. "
"For example, the result of an eval statement is not allowed to be "
"boolean. If search time evaluation of the expression is unsuccessful for "
"a given event, eval erases the value in the result field."
msgstr "执行任意表达式计算，提供数学运算、字符串运算和布尔运算。eval 结果写入指定目标字段中，该字段可以是新字段或现有字段。如果存在目标字段，则该字段的值将替换为 eval 结果。在运行搜索前将检查表达式的语法，如果表达式无效，将引发异常。例如，eval 语句的执行结果不能为布尔类型。如果指定事件的表达式搜索时间计算失败，eval 将消除结果字段中的值。"

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:2436 
msgid ""
"Performs k-means clustering on select fields (or all numerical fields if "
"empty).  Events in the same cluster are \\\n"
"moved next to each other.  You have the option to display the cluster "
"number for each event. The centroid of each cluster is also \\\n"
"be displayed (with an option to disable it)."
msgstr ""
"对所选字段执行 K-均值聚类(如果为空白，则对所有数值型字段执行)。同一群集中的事件将\\\n"
"彼此相邻移动。您可根据需要显示每个事件的群集数。每个群集的中心也将\\\n"
"显示(可用一个选项来禁用它)。"

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:2433 
msgid "Performs k-means clustering on selected fields."
msgstr "对所选字段执行 K-均值聚类。"

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:4220 
msgid "Performs set operations on subsearches."
msgstr "对 subsearch 执行设置操作。"

#: /Users/thopayto/Projects/splunkcore-web-ui/packages/admin-user-xp/src/features/sourcetypes/i18n/messages.ts:102 
#: /Users/thopayto/Projects/splunkcore-web-ui/web_v2/search_mrsparkle/exposed/js/views/sourcetypes/EditDialog.js:9 
msgid ""
"Performs simple key=value field extractions based on a default regular "
"expression."
msgstr "执行基于默认正则表达式的简单的 \"key=value\" 字段提取。"

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:5691 
msgid ""
"Performs statistical queries on indexed fields in tsidx files. You can "
"select from TSIDX data in several different ways:"
"                                  \\p\\\\\n"
"1. Normal index data: If you do not supply a FROM clause, we will select "
"from index data in the same way as search. You are restricted to "
"selecting       \\\n"
"from your allowed indexes by role, and you can control exactly which "
"indexes you select from in the WHERE clause. If no indexes are mentioned"
"          \\\n"
"in the WHERE clause search, we will use your default set of indexes. By "
"default, role-based search filters are applied, but can be turned off in "
"limits.conf. \\\n"
"ADVANCED: When the Splunk software indexes data, it segments each event "
"into raw tokens using rules specified in segmenters.conf.    \\\n"
"You may end up with raw tokens that are actually key-value pairs "
"separated by an arbitrary delimiter such as a '='         \\\n"
"symbol. The following search uses the 'walklex' command to find the raw "
"tokens in your index, along with their count:      \\\n"
"'| walklex index=<target-index> | where NOT like(term, \"%::%\") | stats "
"sum(count) by term'                                 \\\n"
"You can use the PREFIX directive in conjunction with 'tstats' to "
"aggregate and group-by these values within the raw        \\\n"
"tokens in your index. For example, say you have a set of raw tokens that "
"feature a numeric value prefixed by 'kpbs=',      \\\n"
"such as kbps=10 or kbps=333. If you run <tstats-func>(PREFIX(kbps)) on "
"those tokens, the  processor returns '=10' and      \\\n"
"'=333', which isn't exactly what you want, because many tstats "
"aggregation functions require purely numeric values.        \\\n"
"So you adjust your search to include the delimiter and run <tstats-"
"func>(PREFIX(kbps=)) on those tokens. This returns      \\\n"
"values of '10' and '333', which are perfect for tstats aggregation "
"functions. \\p\\\\\n"
"2. Data manually collected with 'tscollect': Select from your namespace "
"with 'FROM <namespace>'. If you supplied no namespace to tscollect, the "
"data      \\\n"
"was collected into the dispatch directory of that job. In that case, you "
"would select from that data with 'FROM sid=<tscollect-job-id>'"
"                \\p\\\\\n"
"3. An accelerated datamodel: Select from this accelerated datamodel with "
"'FROM datamodel=<datamodel-name>'"
"                                                \\\n"
"You can provide any number of aggregates to perform, and also have the "
"option of providing a filtering query using the WHERE keyword. This query"
" looks    \\\n"
"like a normal query you would use in the search processor. You can also "
"provide any number of GROUPBY fields. If you are grouping by _time, you "
"should    \\\n"
"supply a timespan with 'span' for grouping the time buckets. This "
"timespan looks like any normal timespan in Splunk, like '1hr' or '3d'. It"
" also supports 'auto'.     \\p\\\\\n"
"Arguments:"
"                                                                                                                                                "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"\"prestats\": This simply outputs the answer in prestats format, in case "
"you want to pipe the results to a"
"                                                  \\i\\\\\n"
"different type of processor that takes prestats output, like chart or "
"timechart. This is very useful for                                      "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"creating graphs"
"                                                                                                                               "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"\"local\": If you set this to true it forces the processor to only be run"
" on the search head."
"                                                               \\i\\\\\n"
"\"append\": Only valid in prestats mode, this allows tstats to be run to "
"add results to an existing set of"
"                                                  \\i\\\\\n"
"results, instead of generating them."
"                                                                                                            "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"\"summariesonly\": Only applies when selecting from an accelerated "
"datamodel.  When false (default),"
"                                                        \\i\\\\\n"
"Splunk will generate results from both summarized data, as well as for "
"data that is not                                                  \\i\\\\"
"\n"
"summarized. For data not summarized as TSIDX data, the full search "
"behavior will be used                                                 "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"against the original index data.  If set to true, 'tstats' will only "
"generate results from the                                           "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"TSIDX data that has been automatically generated by the acceleration, and"
" nonsummarized data                                             \\i\\\\\n"
"will not be provided."
"                                                                                                                    "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"\"include_reduced_buckets\": Only applies when TSIDX reduction is enabled"
" by setting enableTsidxReduction = true in indexes.conf."
"                           \\i\\\\\n"
"When include_reduced_buckets = false, Splunk generates results only from "
"buckets that are not reduced                          \\i\\\\\n"
"The default for this setting is \"false\"."
"                                                                                       "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"\"allow_old_summaries\": Only applies when selecting from an accelerated "
"datamodel.  When false"
"                                                             \\i\\\\\n"
"(default), Splunk only provides results from summary directories when "
"those directories are up-to-date.                            \\i\\\\\n"
"In other words, if the datamodel definition has changed, we do not use "
"those summary directories                                   \\i\\\\\n"
"which are older than the new definition when producing output from "
"tstats. This default ensures                                    \\i\\\\\n"
"that the output from tstats will always reflect your current "
"configuration. If this is instead                                     "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"set to true, then tstats will use both current summary data as well as "
"summary data that was                                       \\i\\\\\n"
"generated prior to the definition change. Essentially this is an advanced"
" performance                                              \\i\\\\\n"
"feature for cases where you know that the old summaries are \"good "
"enough\".                                                         \\i\\\\"
"\n"
"\"use_summary_index_values\": When this argument is set to 'false' "
"(default), 'tstats' interprets events in summary index"
"                                  \\i\\\\\n"
"buckets that contain prestats-prefixed fields as literal fields. When "
"this argument is set to 'true',                             \\i\\\\\n"
"'tstats' treats those prestats-prefixed fields as partial aggregates "
"(which is another way to refer                               \\i\\\\\n"
"to prestats data). The 'tstats' command interprets these partial "
"aggregates in a manner similar to                                \\i\\\\"
"\n"
"the way that the 'stats' command processes partial aggregates. The "
"'tstats' command then does a                                   \\i\\\\\n"
"fallback search for the buckets where the prestats fields are found, "
"calling an equivalent 'stats'                                \\i\\\\\n"
"search only for those buckets. Enable this setting when you want 'tstats'"
" to return the same results                              \\i\\\\\n"
"that an equivalent 'stats' search would return, such that it interprets "
"values encoded as partial                                 \\i\\\\\n"
"aggregates. When 'use_summary_index_values=true', 'tstats' searches might"
" perform slower, but their                               \\i\\\\\n"
"result sets will have parity with the result sets of corresponding "
"'stats' searches. When this                                    \\i\\\\\n"
"argument is set to 'false', 'tstats' simply looks at the 'tsidx' file and"
" does not perform additional                             \\i\\\\\n"
"interpretation of partial aggregates.    \\p\\\\\n"
"NOTE: The 'replace_*_with_tstats' family of optimizers (such as "
"'replace_stats_cmds_with_tstats'),                                \\i\\\\"
"\n"
"automatically sets this argument to 'true' on a corresponding 'tstats' "
"search so that the optimized                               \\i\\\\\n"
"search is functionally equivalent to the original.    \\p\\\\\n"
"\"chunk_size\": Advanced option. This argument controls how many events "
"are retrieved at a time within"
"                                                      \\i\\\\\n"
"a single TSIDX file when answering queries. The default is 10000000. Only"
" consider supplying a lower                                        "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"value for this if you find a particular query is using too much memory. "
"The case that could cause this                                      "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"would be an excessively high cardinality split-by, such as grouping by "
"several fields that have a very                                      "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"large amount of distinct values. Setting this value too low, however, can"
" negatively impact the overall                                     "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"runtime of your query. If set below 10000, the value will be defaulted to"
" 10000000.                                                         "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"\"fillnull_value\": This argument sets a user-specified value that the "
"tstats command substitutes for null values for"
"                                       \\i\\\\\n"
"any field within its group-by field list. Null values include field "
"values that are missing from                                            "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"a subset of the returned events as well as field values that are missing "
"from all of the returned                                           "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"events. If you do not provide a 'fillnull_value' argument, the tstats "
"command omits rows for events                                         "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"with one or more null field values from its search results."
"                                                                                 "
"\\p\\\\\n"
"NOTE: Except in 'append=t' mode, this is a generating processor, so it "
"must be the first command in a search."
msgstr ""
"对 tsidx 文件中的索引字段执行统计查询。您可以通过多种不同方式从 TSIDX 数据中选择:                                  \\p\\\\\n"
"1. 普通索引数据: 如果未提供 FROM 子句，则将使用与搜索相同的方式从索引数据中选择。您只能按角色       \\\n"
"从允许的索引中进行选择，且可以精确控制在 WHERE 子句中从哪些索引中进行选择。如果没有\\\n"
"WHERE 子句中所述的索引，则将使用默认索引集。默认情况下，将应用基于角色的搜索过滤器，但可以在 limits.conf 中关闭此选项。\\p\\\\\n"
"高级: 当 Splunk 软件索引数据时，该软件会使用 egmenters.conf 中指定的规则，将各事件拆分到原始标记中。    \\\n"
"您可能会得到原始标记，这些标记实际上是通过任意分隔符(例如 '=' 标记) 分隔开来的键值对。         \\\n"
"以下搜索使用 'walklex' 命令查找索引中的原始标记，以及相应的计数:      \\\n"
"'| walklex index=<target-index> | where NOT like(term, \"%::%\") | stats sum(count) by term'                                 \\\n"
"您可以使用将前缀指令和 'tstats' 结合使用以聚合并将这些值分组到索引中的原始标记中。        \\\n"
"例如，假设您有一组原始标记，其数字值前缀为 'kpbs='，例如 kbps=10 或 kbps=333。       \\\n"
"如果您在这些标记上运行 <tstats-func>(PREFIX(kbps))，处理器会返回 '=10' 和      \\\n"
"'=333'，这并不是您想要的精确值，因为很多 tstats 聚合函数需要纯数字值。        \\\n"
"因此，您要调整搜索以将分隔符包括在内并在这些标记上运行 <tstats-func>(PREFIX(kbps=))。这样会返回      \\\n"
"值 '10' 和 '333'，这是 tstats 聚合函数想要的精确结果。\\p\\\\\n"
"2. 使用 'tscollect' 手动收集的数据: 使用 'FROM <namespace>' 从命名空间中选择。 如没有向 tscollect 提供命名空间，则会将数据      \\\n"
"收集到该任务的 dispatch 目录中。 在此情况下，将使用 'FROM sid=<tscollect-job-id>'从该数据中选择                \\p\\\\\n"
"3. 加速的数据模型: 使用 'FROM datamodel=<datamodel-name>' 从此加速的数据模型中选择                                                \\\n"
"可提供要执行的任意数量的聚合，也可选择使用 WHERE 关键字提供过滤查询。 此查询和    \\\n"
"您在搜索处理器中使用的普通查询近似。也可提供任意数量的 GROUPBY 字段。如分组 by _time，应\\\n"
"提供一个时间跨度以分组时间数据桶。此时间跨度和 Splunk 中的任何普通时间跨度近似，如 '1hr' 或 '3d'。此外，还支持 'auto'。     \\p\\\\\n"
"参数:                                                                                                                                                \\i\\\\\n"
"\"prestats\": 如果要通过管道将结果传递到                                                  \\i\\\\\n"
"采用 prestats 输出的不同类型的处理器，如 chart 或 timechart，则此选项只会以 prestats 格式输出答案。这对于                                      \\i\\\\\n"
"新建图形非常有用                                                                                                                               \\i\\\\\n"
"\"local\": 如果将此项设置为 true，则会强制处理器仅在搜索头上运行。                                                               \\i\\\\\n"
"\"append\": 仅在 prestats 模式下有效，允许运行 tstats 以将结果添加到现有                                                  \\i\\\\\n"
"结果集，而不是生成结果集。                                                                                                            \\i\\\\\n"
"\"summariesonly\": 仅适用于从加速的数据模型中选择的情况。为默认的 false 时，                                                        \\i\\\\\n"
"Splunk 将从汇总数据和未                                                  \\i\\\\\n"
"汇总数据生成结果。对于未汇总为 TSIDX 数据的数据，将                                                 \\i\\\\\n"
"对原始索引数据使用完全搜索行为。如果设置为 true，'tstats' 将仅通过加速自动生成的                                           \\i\\\\\n"
" TSIDX 数据生成结果，                                             \\i\\\\\n"
"不提供未汇总数据。                                                                                                                    \\i\\\\\n"
"\"allow_old_summaries\": 仅适用于从加速的数据模型中选择的情况。为默认的 false 时，                                                             \\i\\\\\n"
"\"include_reduced_buckets\": 仅当在 indexes.conf 中设置 enableTsidxReduction = true 启用 TSIDX 减少时适用。                            \\i\\\\\n"
"当 include_reduced_buckets = false 时，Splunk 会仅从未减少的数据桶中生成结果                          \\i\\\\\n"
"默认设置为 \"false\"。                                                                                       \\i\\\\\n"
"Splunk 仅在目录为最新时提供来自汇总目录的结果。                            \\i\\\\\n"
"即，如果数据模型定义更改，我们从 tstats 进行导出时，不使用                                   \\i\\\\\n"
"比新定义旧的那些汇总目录。此默认设置可确保                                    \\i\\\\\n"
"从 tstats 输出的内容始终反映当前配置。如果改为设置                                     \\i\\\\\n"
"为 true，tstats 将使用当前汇总数据和定义更改前                                     \\i\\\\\n"
"生成的汇总数据。实际上，这是一种高级性能功能，适用于您已了解旧汇总已“足够好”的情况。                                                         \\i\\\\\n"
"\"chunk_size\": 高级选项。此参数控制回答查询时，在                                                         \\i\\\\\n"
"单个 TSIDX 文件中一次检索的事件数量。默认为 10000000。如果发现某特殊查询使用内存过多，仅为此参数提供较低                                                         \\i\\\\\n"
"值。导致这一结果的情况                                                         \\i\\\\\n"
"可能是基数拆分过高，例如按拥有                                     \\i\\\\\n"
"大量非重复值的多个字段进行分组。但将此值设置过低将对查询的整个                                     \\i\\\\\n"
"运行时产生负面影响。如果设置为 10000 以下，则该值默认为 10000000。                                                         \\i\\\\\n"
"\"fillnull_value\": 此参数设置一个用户指定的值，tstats 命令用其替换分类依据列表中的任何字段                                       \\i\\\\\n"
"的空值。空值包括返回的事件子集的丢失字段值                                            \\i\\\\\n"
"以及所有返回的事件丢失的字段值。                                           \\i\\\\\n"
"如果您没有提供 'fillnull_value' 参数，tstats 命令会省略搜索结果中                                         \\i\\\\\n"
"具有一个或多个空字段值的事件行。                                                                                 \\p\\\\\n"
"注意: 除了在 'append=t' 模式中，这是一个生成处理器，因此它必须是搜索中的第一个命令。"

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:5620 
msgid ""
"Performs statistics on indexed fields in tsidx files, which could come "
"from normal index data, tscollect data, or accelerated datamodels."
msgstr "对 tsidx 文件中的索引字段执行统计，这些文件可能来自普通索引数据、tscollect 数据或加速的数据模型。"

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:5402 
msgid ""
"Performs statistics on the measurement, metric_name and dimension fields "
"in metric indexes. Supports historical and real-time search."
msgstr "就指标索引中的评估、metric_name 和维度字段进行统计。支持历史搜索和实时搜索。"

#: default/searchbnf.conf.in:5508 
msgid ""
"Performs statistics on the measurement, metric_name, and  \\\n"
"dimension fields in metric indexes. The mstats command is \\\n"
"optimized for searches over one or more metric_name values, \\\n"
"rather than searches over all metric_name values. It supports \\\n"
"both historical and real-time searches. For a real-time search \\\n"
"with a time window, mstats runs a historical search first that \\\n"
"backfills the data.\\p\\\\\n"
"The mstats command is a generating command, except when it is \\\n"
"in 'append=t' mode. As such, it must be the first command in a \\\n"
"search.\\p\\\\\n"
"In 'chart=t' mode, the output is formatted in format suitable for \\\n"
"charting, similar to the chart and timechart commands. \\\n"
"Charting mode is not compatible with append mode or prestats mode.\\p\\\\"
"\n"
"If the <stats-func> based syntax is used, the filter specified after \\\n"
"the WHERE clause cannot filter on metric_name. Any metric_name \\\n"
"filtering is performed based on the metric_name fields specified \\\n"
"by the <stats-func> argument.  If the <stats-func-value> syntax \\\n"
"is used, the WHERE clause *must* filter on metric_name (wildcards are "
"ok). \\\n"
"It is recommended to use the <stats-func> syntax when possible.  \\\n"
"The <stats-func-value> syntax is needed for cases where a single metric "
"may be \\\n"
"represented by several different metric names (e.g. \"cpu.util\" and "
"\"cpu.utilization\"). \\p\\\\\n"
"You cannot blend the <stats-func> syntax with the <stats-func-value> "
"syntax in a single mstats command. \\p\\\\\n"
"Arguments: \\p\\\\\n"
"\"<stats-func>\": A list of stats functions to compute for given  \\\n"
"metric_names. These are written as \\\n"
"<function1>(metric_name1) <function2>(metric_name2) ... \\p\\\\\n"
"\"<stats-func-value>\": A list of stats functions to compute on \\\n"
"metric values (_value).  These are written as \\\n"
"<function1>(_value) <function2>(_value) ... \\p\\\\\n"
"\"<logical-expression>\": An expression describing the filters \\\n"
"that are applied to your search. Includes time and \\\n"
"search modifiers, comparison expressions, and index \\\n"
"expressions. This expression cannot filter on \\\n"
"metric_name if the <stats-func> syntax is used, but \\\n"
"must filter on metric_name if the <stats-func-value> \\\n"
"syntax is used.\\p\\\\\n"
"\"<field-list>\": Specifies one or more fields to group the \\\n"
"results by. Required when using the 'BY' or \\\n"
"'GROUPBY' clause. \\p\\\\\n"
"\"prestats\": Returns the results in prestats format. You can pipe \\\n"
"the results into commands that consume the prestats \\\n"
"formatted data, such as chart or timechart, and \\\n"
"output aggregate calculations. This is useful for \\\n"
"creating graphs. Default is prestats=false. \\p\\\\\n"
"\"append\": Valid only when \"prestats=true\". This argument adds \\\n"
"the results of the mstats run to an existing set of \\\n"
"results instead of generating new results. Default is \\\n"
"\"append=false\". \\p\\\\\n"
"\"chart\":  Valid only when \"prestats=false\".  When set to \"true\", \\"
"\n"
"the mstats command emits output in a format similar to \\\n"
"chart (when no span given) and timechart (when span is given). \\\n"
"When no span is provided, chart mode requires specifying \\\n"
"one or two grouping fields, the first of which specifies \\\n"
"the x-axis field, and the latter the series split field. \\\n"
"When a span is provided, chart mode supports at most one \\\n"
"groupby field, which would be used as the series splitting \\\n"
"field.  Default is \"chart=false\". \\p\\\\\n"
"The options that start with \"chart.\" are only valid in charting mode "
"(chart=true). \\p\\\\\n"
"\"chart.limit\":  Limits for the number of series \\\n"
"(columns) generated.  Same behavior as the chart/timechart \\\n"
"limit option.  0 means no limit.  Optionally prefixed by \"top\" or \\\n"
"\"bottom\" to determine which series to select.  A number without a "
"prefix \\\n"
"means the same thing as having \"top\" as the prefix.  Default is 10. "
"\\p\\\\\n"
"\"chart.agg\":    Specifies the aggregation \\\n"
"functions used to select which series to show.  Same behavior \\\n"
"as the chart/timechart agg option.  Default is \"sum\". \\p\\\\\n"
"chart.(\"usenull\"/\"nullstr\"/\"useother\"/\"otherstr\"):  Same behavior"
" as \\\n"
"chart/timechart options of the same name. \\p\\\\\n"
"\"backfill\": Valid only with windowed real-time searches. When \\\n"
"set to \"true\", the mstats command runs a historical \\\n"
"search to backfill the on-disk indexed data before \\\n"
"searching the in-memory real-time data. Default is \\\n"
"\"backfill=true\".\\p\\\\\n"
"\"update_period\": Valid only with real-time searches. Specifies \\\n"
"how frequently, in milliseconds, the real-time \\\n"
"summary for the mstats command is updated. By \\\n"
"default, update_period=0, which is 1 second. A \\\n"
"larger number means less frequent reads of the \\\n"
"summary and less impact on index processing.\\p\\\\\n"
"\"fillnull_value\": This argument sets a user-specified value \\\n"
"that the mstats command substitutes for null values \\\n"
"for any field within its group-by field list. Null \\\n"
"values include field values that are missing from \\\n"
"a subset of the returned events as well as field \\\n"
"values that are missing from all of the returned \\\n"
"events. If you do not provide a 'fillnull_value' \\\n"
"argument, the tstats command omits rows for events \\\n"
"with one or more null field values from its search \\\n"
"results. \\p\\\\\n"
"\"chunk_size\": Advanced option. This argument controls how many "
"timeseries \\\n"
"are retrieved at a time within a single metric TSIDX file when \\\n"
"answering queries. The default is 10000000. Only consider \\\n"
"supplying a lower value for this if you find a particular \\\n"
"query is using too much memory. The case that could cause \\\n"
"this would be an excessively high cardinality split-by, such \\\n"
"as grouping by several fields that have a very large amount of \\\n"
"of distinct values. Setting this value too low, however, can \\\n"
"negatively impact the overall runtime of your query. If set \\\n"
"below 10000, the value will be defaulted to 10000000. \\p\\\\\n"
"\"every\": This argument controls how often the Splunk software computes "
"\\\n"
"an aggregation point using the aggregation window specified \\\n"
"by the 'span' argument. When you use 'every' along with 'span', \\\n"
"you can skip values by searching discrete time intervals. \\\n"
"The 'every' argument is valid only when 'span' is set to a \\\n"
"valid value other than 'auto'. Set 'every' to a valid timespan \\\n"
"that is greater than the 'span' timespan."
msgstr ""
"就指标索引中的评估、metric_name 和\\\n"
"维度字段进行统计。mstats 命令经过了优化，\\\n"
"可以只针对一个或多个 metric_name 值进行搜索，\\\n"
"而不会搜索所有 metric_name 值。它既支持\\\n"
"历史搜索也支持实时搜索。对于带时间窗口的\\\n"
"实时搜索，mstats 会首先运行历史搜索\\\n"
"以回填数据。\\p\\\\\n"
"mstats 命令是一种生成命令，但当它\\\n"
"处于 'append=t' 模式时除外。因此，它必须是搜索中的第一个\\\n"
"命令。\\p\\\\\n"
"在 'chart = t' 模式下，输出采用适用于制作图表的格式，\\\n"
"类似于 chart 和 timechart 命令。\\\n"
"制作图表模式与追加模式或 prestats 模式不兼容。\\p\\\\\n"
"如果使用基于 <stats-func> 的语法，WHERE 子句之后指定的过滤器\\\n"
"无法过滤 metric_name。所有 metric_name 过滤\\\n"
"都基于由 <stats-func> 参数指定的 metric_name 字段。\\\n"
"如果使用 <stats-func-value> 语法，\\\n"
"WHERE 语句*必须*过滤 metric_name (通配符没问题)。\\\n"
"建议尽量使用 <stats-func> 语法。\\\n"
"当单一指标可能由几个不同的指标名称\\\n"
"(如 \"cpu.util\" 和 \"cpu.utilization\")表示时需要使用 <stats-func-value> 语法。\\p\\\\\n"
"您不可将 <stats-func> 语法和单一 mstats 命令中的 <stats-func-value> 语法混合使用。\\p\\\\\n"
"参数: \\p\\\\\n"
"\"<stats-func>\": 用于计算指定 metric_names 的 stats 函数列表。\\\n"
"这些函数写作\\\n"
"<function1>(metric_name1) <function2>(metric_name2) ... \\p\\\\\n"
"\"<stats-func-value>\": 用于计算指标值(_value)的 stats 函数列表。\\\n"
"这些函数写作\\\n"
"<function1>(_value) <function2>(_value) ... \\p\\\\\n"
"\"<logical-expression>\": 描述应用于搜索的过滤器\\\n"
"的表达式。包括时间和\\\n"
"搜索调节器、比较表达式和索引\\\n"
"表达式。如果使用 <stats-func> 语法，\\\n"
"则此表达式无法过滤 \\\n"
"metric_name。但是如果\\\n"
"使用 <stats-func-value> 语法，必须过滤 metric_name。\\p\\\\\n"
"\"<field-list>\": 指定一个或多个字段作为结果的\\\n"
"分组标准。当使用 'BY' 或 'GROUPBY' \\\n"
"子句时为必选项。\\p\\\\\n"
"\"prestats\": 以 prestats 格式返回结果。您可以将结果传递给\\\n"
"处理 prestats 格式化数据 (如图表或\\\n"
"时间表) 的命令，并\\\n"
"输出聚合计算结果。这对于新建图形\\\n"
"十分有用。默认设置为 prestats=false。\\p\\\\\n"
"\"append\": 仅当 \"prestats=true\" 时有效。此参数\\\n"
"运行 mstats 命令并将结果添加到现有的\\\n"
"结果集，而非生成新的结果。默认设置为 \\\n"
"\"append=false\"。\\p\\\\\n"
"“chart”: 仅在 \"prestats=false\" 时有效。当设置为 \"true\" 时，\\\n"
"mstats 命令以类似于图表(未指定跨度)\\\n"
"和时间表(指定跨度)的格式输出结果。\\\n"
"如果未提供跨度，则图表模式需要指定\\\n"
"一个或两个分组字段，第一个指定\\\n"
"x 轴字段，而第二个指定系列拆分字段。\\\n"
"如果提供了跨度，图表模式最多支持一个\\\n"
"groupby 字段，且该字段用作系列拆分\\\n"
"字段。默认值为 \"chart=false\"。\\p\\\\\n"
"以 \"chart.\" 开头的选项仅在图表模式下有效(chart=true)。\\p\\\\\n"
"\"chart.limit\": 限制生成的系列(列)\\\n"
"数。与图表/时间表限制选项的行为\\\n"
"相同。0 表示没有限制。可以选择以 \"top\" 或 \"bottom\" 为\\\n"
"前缀，以确定要选择的系列。没有前缀的数字\\\n"
"与以 \"top\" 为前缀的含义相同。默认值为 10。\\p\\\\\n"
"\"chart.agg\": 指定用于选择\\\n"
"要显示的系列的聚合函数。行为与图表/时间表\\\n"
"的 agg 选项相同。默认值为 \"sum\"。\\p\\\\\n"
"chart. (\"usenull\"/\"nullstr\"/\"useother\"/\"otherstr\"): 与具有相同名称的\\\n"
"图表/时间表选项的行为相同。\\p\\\\\n"
"\"backfill\": 只在执行窗口的实时搜索时有效。当\\\n"
"设置为 \"true\" 时，在搜索内存中的实时数据前，\\\n"
"mstats 命令会运行历史搜索以回填磁盘上\\\n"
"的索引数据。默认设置为\\\n"
"\"backfill=true\"。\\p\\\\\n"
"\"update_period\": 只对实时搜索有效。\\\n"
"指定 mstats 命令的实时摘要的\\\n"
"更新频率(以毫秒为单位)。\\\n"
"默认设置为 update_period=0，也就是 1 秒。\\\n"
"数字越大表示摘要读取频率越小，\\\n"
"对索引处理的影响也越小。\\p\\\\\n"
"\"fillnull_value\": 此参数设置一个用户指定的值，\\\n"
"mstats 命令用其替换分类依据列表中\\\n"
"的任何字段的空值。空值\\\n"
"包括返回的事件子集\\\n"
"的丢失字段值以及所有\\\n"
"返回的事件丢失的字段值。\\\n"
"如果您没有提供 'fillnull_value' \\\n"
"参数，tstats 命令会省略搜索\\\n"
"结果中具有一个或多个空字段值的\\\n"
"事件行。\\p\\\\\n"
"\"chunk_size\": 高级选项。此参数控制回答查询时，\\\n"
"在单个 TSIDX 文件中一次检索的\\\n"
"时间系列数。默认为 10000000。只有在\\\n"
"发现特定查询使用内存过多时，才可以考虑\\\n"
"为此参数设置较低的值。导致这一结果\\\n"
"的情况可能是基数拆分过高，例如\\\n"
"按拥有大量非重复值的多个字段进行分组。\\\n"
"但将此值设置过低，则会\\\n"
"对查询的整体运行时间产生负面影响。如果\\\n"
"设置的值小于 10000，则其值就采用默认值 10000000。\\p\\\\\n"
"\"every\": 此参数控制 Splunk 软件使用\\\n"
"由 'span' 参数指定的聚合窗口计算\\\n"
"聚合点的频率。当同时使用 'every' 和 'span'，\\\n"
"您可以通过搜索离散的时间间隔来跳过值。\\\n"
"仅当 'span' 设置为除 'auto' 以外的其他有效值时，\\\n"
"'every' 参数才有效。将 'every' 设置为大于 'span' \\\n"
"时间跨度的有效时间跨度。"

